<title>GERMANY: Rheinmetall mulls capital hike post STN buy.</title>
<headline>Rheinmetall mulls capital hike post STN buy.</headline>
<dateline>BREMEN, Germany 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>German defence group Rheinmetall AG said on Thursday it was considering an equity increase after it led an Anglo-German consortium to take over STN Atlas from bankrupt shipbuilders Bremer Vulkan AG.</p>
<p>Chief executive Hans Brauner told reporters financing for the 550 million mark deal, in which Rheinmetall and Badenwerk will share a 51 percent stake of STN Atlas and British Aerospace will take 49 percent, was secure.</p>
<p>But, he added, a capital increase was &quot;probable&quot;. He gave no indication of how big any rights issue might be.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
